id: pm-web-2ut6
title: Spanish (es) locale for package-owned UI strings
description: "Add a Spanish (es) locale catalog for the package-owned SPA UI strings (auth, nav, banners, settings, consent, dialog, error mapping). Register es in locale resolution and the settings language selector (English/Deutsch/Espanol). Legal pages remain an operator concern and are not translated by this package."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: es,i18n,locale,settings
created_at: "2026-07-17T06:52:56.558Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:04:17.286Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:04:17.285Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: es.json catalog exists with all 110 en keys translated to natural Spanish (usted register); es registered in SUPPORTED_LOCALES and resolveLocale (es and es-MX prefix match); settings language selector offers English/Deutsch/Espanol; npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm test green; catalog-parity test covers es automatically
release: 2026.7.18
resolution: Work completed and released in 2026.7.18. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.7.18 instead of the current release notes.
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.7.18 heading it actually shipped in, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Item remained in_progress with no activity after its work shipped, so the delivery was absent from the changelog while still counting as open work in every fleet audit."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the Spanish locale, shipped as public/src/i18n/es.json was completed and released in 2026.7.18, but the item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: ""
